 "title": "Resources for the development sector",
 "excerpt": "Regulators, foreign funding rules, coordination bodies, donors, data sources, funding portals, job boards and a sector glossary for Bangladesh.",
 "content": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A practical toolkit for people who work in Bangladesh&#8217;s development and humanitarian sector: the regulators you deal with, the rules on foreign funding, where coordination happens, who funds what, and where to find data, grants and jobs. Every link goes to the official source or a recognised reference. Last checked: 7 November 2026.</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:15px\"><strong>Jump to:</strong> <a href=\"#regulation\">Registration and regulation</a> · <a href=\"#fdva\">Foreign funding rules at a glance</a> · <a href=\"#coordination\">Coordination and networks</a> · <a href=\"#donors\">Funders and donor partners</a> · <a href=\"#portals\">Where to find funding</a> · <a href=\"#data\">Data and evidence</a> · <a href=\"#jobs\">Job boards</a> · <a href=\"#glossary\">Sector glossary</a></p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"regulation\">Registration and regulation</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Which office you register with depends on what you do and where your money comes from. Many organisations hold more than one registration.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Regulator</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://ngoab.portal.gov.bd/\" rel=\"noopener\">NGO Affairs Bureau (NGOAB)</a></td><td>Registration of NGOs that receive foreign donations, and approval of every foreign-funded project. Sits under the Prime Minister&#8217;s Office.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microcredit_Regulatory_Authority\" rel=\"noopener\">Microcredit Regulatory Authority (MRA)</a></td><td>Licensing and supervision of NGOs that run microfinance. No NGO may run microcredit without an MRA licence.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.dss.gov.bd/\" rel=\"noopener\">Department of Social Services (DSS)</a></td><td>Registration of voluntary social welfare organisations under the 1961 ordinance. Common for local organisations working with local funds.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.roc.gov.bd/\" rel=\"noopener\">Registrar of Joint Stock Companies and Firms (RJSC)</a></td><td>Registration of societies and not-for-profit companies (Section 28 companies under the Companies Act).</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://legalseba.com/bd-articles/ngo-formation-primary-regulatory-authorities-in-bangladesh/\" rel=\"noopener\">NGO formation and regulators: a plain guide</a></td><td>Secondary explainer comparing the registration routes. Check details with the regulator before you apply.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fdva\">Foreign funding rules at a glance</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The <a href=\"https://www.icnl.org/research/library/bangladesh_fdva/\">Foreign Donations (Voluntary Activities) Regulation Act 2016</a> governs all foreign money for voluntary work. The main points, from the text of the Act and the NGO Affairs Bureau:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Register first.</strong> An organisation may not run foreign-funded activities without registering with the Bureau (section 3). Registration lasts 10 years.</li>\n<li><strong>Renew early.</strong> Apply for renewal six months before your registration expires (section 4).</li>\n<li><strong>Every project needs approval.</strong> Foreign funds may not be accepted or spent until the project is approved (section 6). Use <strong>Form FD-6</strong> for a regular project proposal.</li>\n<li><strong>Emergencies are fast-tracked.</strong> Relief after floods, cyclones and other disasters uses <strong>Form FD-7</strong>. The Act says suitable applications are approved within 24 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>One-off gifts.</strong> <strong>Form FC-1</strong> covers a one-time foreign contribution, for example for Ramadan or Eid distributions.</li>\n<li><strong>Overheads are capped.</strong> Administrative costs may not exceed 20% of a project&#8217;s approved budget (section 6).</li>\n<li><strong>Use one mother account.</strong> All foreign donations must come through a single designated account at a scheduled bank (section 9).</li>\n<li><strong>Keep records.</strong> Keep expenditure vouchers for five years after a project ends, and send annual activity and accounts statements (sections 12 and 13).</li>\n<li><strong>Appeals.</strong> You can appeal a Bureau decision to the Prime Minister&#8217;s Office within 30 working days (section 17).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"color:#6b6f76;font-size:14px\">This is a summary, not legal advice. Forms and procedures change: always check the current version on the <a href=\"https://ngoab.portal.gov.bd/\">NGO Affairs Bureau website</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"coordination\">Coordination and networks</h2>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Body</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://response.reliefweb.int/bangladesh/humanitarian-coordination-task-team\" rel=\"noopener\">Humanitarian Coordination Task Team (HCTT)</a></td><td>National forum for disaster response, co-led by the government and the UN. Meeting minutes and terms of reference are public.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://reliefweb.int/organization/iscg-cxb\" rel=\"noopener\">Inter Sector Coordination Group (ISCG), Cox&#8217;s Bazar</a></td><td>Coordinates the Rohingya refugee response across sectors and agencies, and publishes the Joint Response Plan.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://response.reliefweb.int/bangladesh\" rel=\"noopener\">Bangladesh response page on ReliefWeb Response</a></td><td>Sector and working group pages, contact lists, meeting minutes and reports for the humanitarian system in Bangladesh.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://bdplatform4sdgs.net/profile/association-of-development-agencies-in-bangladesh-adab/\" rel=\"noopener\">Association of Development Agencies in Bangladesh (ADAB)</a></td><td>One of the oldest NGO networks in Bangladesh.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://bdplatform4sdgs.net/profile/federation-of-ngos-in-bangladesh-fnb/\" rel=\"noopener\">Federation of NGOs in Bangladesh (FNB)</a></td><td>Umbrella body that represents NGOs in dialogue with the government.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://bdplatform4sdgs.net/\" rel=\"noopener\">Bangladesh Civil Society Platform for SDGs</a></td><td>Network of civil society organisations tracking the Sustainable Development Goals, with profiles of member organisations.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"donors\">Funders and donor partners</h2>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The main multilateral and bilateral partners with country programmes in Bangladesh. Their country pages list current projects, procurement notices and contacts.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Funder</th><th>What to look for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/bangladesh\" rel=\"noopener\">World Bank in Bangladesh</a></td><td>Largest development lender. Project documents, procurement and country reports.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.adb.org/where-we-work/bangladesh\" rel=\"noopener\">Asian Development Bank: Bangladesh</a></td><td>Loans and grants for infrastructure, energy, urban services and skills.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://bangladesh.un.org/\" rel=\"noopener\">United Nations in Bangladesh</a></td><td>The UN country team, its cooperation framework and the agencies working in Bangladesh.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.eeas.europa.eu/delegations/bangladesh_en\" rel=\"noopener\">European Union Delegation to Bangladesh</a></td><td>EU programmes, calls for proposals and local job notices.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.jica.go.jp/english/overseas/bangladesh/\" rel=\"noopener\">JICA Bangladesh</a></td><td>Japan&#8217;s development agency, a major infrastructure and human development partner.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://pksf.org.bd/\" rel=\"noopener\">PKSF (Palli Karma-Sahayak Foundation)</a></td><td>Government-established apex funder that channels money to partner NGOs for livelihoods, microfinance and climate work.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.greenclimate.fund/partners/accredited-entities/pksf\" rel=\"noopener\">Green Climate Fund: PKSF as accredited entity</a></td><td>How Bangladesh accesses Green Climate Fund money through a national entity.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"portals\">Where to find funding</h2>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Portal</th><th>What it lists</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"/funding/\" rel=\"noopener\">Devlens Funding page</a></td><td>Our curated list of open calls for Bangladesh, checked against the funder&#8217;s notice.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.unpartnerportal.org/\" rel=\"noopener\">UN Partner Portal</a></td><td>Where UN agencies such as UNHCR, UNICEF and WFP post calls for NGO partners. Register your organisation once to apply.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/\" rel=\"noopener\">EU Funding and Tenders Portal</a></td><td>Calls for proposals and tenders from the European Union.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://reliefweb.int/country/bgd\" rel=\"noopener\">ReliefWeb: Bangladesh</a></td><td>Reports, appeals and funding updates from humanitarian agencies working in Bangladesh.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"data\">Data and evidence</h2>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://bbs.gov.bd/\" rel=\"noopener\">Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS)</a></td><td>Official statistics: census, labour force survey, household income and expenditure survey, price data.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://data.humdata.org/group/bgd\" rel=\"noopener\">Humanitarian Data Exchange: Bangladesh</a></td><td>Open datasets from humanitarian agencies: admin boundaries, needs, population and response data.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://data.unhcr.org/en/situations/myanmar_refugees\" rel=\"noopener\">UNHCR operational data: Rohingya response</a></td><td>Refugee population figures and documents for the Rohingya response.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://data.worldbank.org/country/bangladesh\" rel=\"noopener\">World Bank open data: Bangladesh</a></td><td>Long-run indicators on the economy, poverty, health and education.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://dhsprogram.com/Countries/Country-Main.cfm?ctry_id=1\" rel=\"noopener\">The DHS Program: Bangladesh</a></td><td>Demographic and Health Survey reports and data.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"/data/\" rel=\"noopener\">Devlens Data page</a></td><td>Key figures we have checked and sourced, updated as new reports come out.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"jobs\">Job boards</h2>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Board</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"/jobs/\" rel=\"noopener\">Devlens Jobs</a></td><td>NGO, INGO and UN roles in Bangladesh, checked every night. Expired roles come off automatically.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://careers.un.org/\" rel=\"noopener\">UN Careers</a></td><td>The UN Secretariat&#8217;s job site. Agencies such as UNICEF, UNDP and WFP run their own career pages.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.impactpool.org/countries/Bangladesh\" rel=\"noopener\">Impactpool: Bangladesh</a></td><td>Development and UN roles in Bangladesh from many employers.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://unjobs.org/duty_stations/bangladesh\" rel=\"noopener\">UNjobs: Bangladesh</a></td><td>Aggregator of UN, INGO and NGO vacancies by duty station.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://reliefweb.int/jobs\" rel=\"noopener\">ReliefWeb jobs</a></td><td>Humanitarian and development vacancies worldwide, filterable by country.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://www.bdjobs.com/\" rel=\"noopener\">Bdjobs</a></td><td>Bangladesh&#8217;s largest job site, with many national NGO circulars.</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"color:#6b6f76;font-size:14px\">Never pay to apply. Genuine employers do not charge application or processing fees.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"glossary\">Sector glossary</h2>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>FD-6, FD-7, FC-1</td><td>NGO Affairs Bureau forms for a regular project, an emergency relief project and a one-time foreign contribution.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>NGOAB</td><td>NGO Affairs Bureau, the regulator for foreign-funded NGOs.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>MRA</td><td>Microcredit Regulatory Authority, which licenses microfinance NGOs.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>FDMN</td><td>Forcibly Displaced Myanmar Nationals, the government&#8217;s term for Rohingya refugees.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>JRP</td><td>Joint Response Plan, the annual appeal for the Rohingya response.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>HCTT / ISCG</td><td>The national disaster coordination forum, and the coordination group for the Rohingya response in Cox&#8217;s Bazar.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CFP, EOI, RFP, ToR</td><td>Call for proposals, expression of interest, request for proposals, and terms of reference.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>NO-A to NO-D</td><td>UN national officer grades, open only to Bangladeshi nationals.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>LDC graduation</td><td>Bangladesh leaving the UN least developed country category, which affects trade preferences and some concessional finance.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Localisation</td><td>Shifting funding and decision-making to national and local organisations.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Know a resource that should be here, or spotted an out-of-date link? <a href=\"/submit/\">Tell us</a>.</p>",
